  <h2>Why we built this</h2>
  <p>
    Most people have no idea how their finances stack up. Bank apps show
    balances, not context. Spreadsheets are intimidating. And serious financial
    tools tend to feel like homework. We wanted the opposite: a fast, friendly
    way to get a real read on your <strong>financial health score</strong> — then
    laugh a little and maybe get motivated to do better.
  </p>
  <p>
    So we built Cooked Finance around one simple question: <em>are you
    financially cooked?</em> Answer four quick inputs — age, income, savings, and
    debt — and you get a 0–100 Cooked Score, a percentile versus other Americans
    your age, a Financial Age, and a personalized (lighthearted) roast.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    Our scoring engine weighs the things that actually matter for long-term
    financial health, in order of impact:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Savings-to-income ratio</strong> — the biggest factor.</li>
    <li><strong>Debt-to-income ratio</strong> — the second-heaviest.</li>
    <li><strong>Net savings</strong> — your savings minus total debt.</li>
    <li><strong>Age-adjusted progress</strong> — how you track against typical milestones.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The benchmarks are inspired by the Federal Reserve's Survey of Consumer
    Finances and Fidelity-style savings guideposts, calibrated to feel realistic.
    Income alone never wins — strong savings and low debt do.
  </p>

  <h2>What we believe</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Privacy first.</strong> Everything runs in your browser. We don't collect, store, or transmit your financial inputs.</li>
    <li><strong>Free, always.</strong> No accounts, no paywalls, no upsells.</li>
    <li><strong>Fun beats fear.</strong> A score you'll share does more good than a lecture you'll ignore.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>One important note</h2>
  <p>
    Cooked Finance is for entertainment and educational purposes only. It is not
    financial advice. For decisions about your specific situation, please talk to
    a qualified financial professional. Questions or feedback? Visit our
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a> — we'd love to hear from you.
  </p>
